{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact 9afe94799d4600713600a2c35de2e0ef5796e3d6 (tree 1c072e8133ee070fb6468582e8a245a7c60e7316), against Main afe0c3190d500f5936e7bd711be67ee4b980b4e0.\n\n1. P2 — Let provenance name the exact recapture or reading used (notes/2026-10-21-capture-with-source.md:59-67, 80-82, 207-209). derivedFrom and the proposed issue captured field accept only facts whose act kind is capture. But a new version is a recapture fact, and a reading is opened by read. A transcript of version 2 cannot cite that version; a summary of a transcript cannot cite the read that produced the transcript. Pointing at the initial capture either cites different bytes or requires following a mutable latest item, losing the exact source. Define an immutable version reference that accepts every supported capture-producing act (or consolidate their act shape), and retain that exact reference through derived readings and issue sources. Witness capture v1, recapture v2, reading of v2, and reading of that reading; later recapture/redaction must not retarget these references.\n\n2. P2 — Identify local-branch content by its own revision, not its base (primary:182-187; CS3). The proposed revision is the base commit, and CS3 requires same-revision refusal for a repeated base and branch. Two different heads or proposed manifests on the same branch can share a base. After the first capture, the documented rule rejects the second despite changed source bytes, and records no identity for the proposed content. Keep base as provenance, give the capture an exact head/tree or canonical manifest/content digest as its revision, and define its repository-qualified external identity. A repeat of identical content should deduplicate; two different proposals from the same base/branch must remain distinct captured versions. Current dap propose reads files against the published destination base (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:1578-1589), which is not a version of the captured branch content.\n\n3. P2 — Preserve source identity when an item is withdrawn (primary:80-83, 140-155). The contract says one item for each source, but the deduplication guard searches only open items. Capture external object X, withdraw it, then redeliver X: capture opens a second item rather than refusing the duplicate. This also lets a routine connector replay bring deliberately withdrawn work back into intake. Specify whether withdrawal keeps a durable source mapping/tombstone, or whether an explicit authorized reopen reuses the same item; distinguish that operation from automatic redelivery. Witness withdrawal followed by duplicate delivery and a subsequent genuine source update. State the revision-history policy as well: equality only with the latest revision is not deduplication of every previously captured revision.\n\nPrimary Source 88f68d40 was read first in full: 246 lines, 13806 bytes, SHA256 88b36922f8d5e390ecf5da880940dc250ef1a119f09db3484afff25ca1d090c8. Checked governing request e5f9fc03 and implementation promise a58d7af1, landed retained-files section 10 and RF4, the imported-identity/ingress/outbox rules, field/fact types, item revisions, roster authority, current CLI proposal behavior, issue/evidence contracts and future view contracts. Prepare binds the exact Source to that request/promise. Source is fresh/live and is the only new path.\n\nThe document/reading/signed-act distinction, imported-author identity as text, external close as observation, connector-as-member model and stated broader current agent authority are sound. Shared capture scope, source display, matter-room exit, follow-up outbox/other channels/CI and CS1-CS4 order after RF1-RF4 are clear. This verdict concerns design only; it does not approve implementation, runtime behavior or provider APIs.\n\nAll 22 copied design/current-contract files match immutable Git bytes and 100644 modes. git diff --check afe0c319 9afe9479 passed. No tests, gate, installation, deployment, publication, shared checkout edits or WIP execution. Evidence root closed before filing this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:88f68d40643402ce5f4b60dfd26913aa0595de7c","binding":"assigned","head":"9afe94799d4600713600a2c35de2e0ef5796e3d6","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:80e7d0cc968743d9f09ef1b98e9792f3db96e5bc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a58d7af150d20915de5f96f4a93b9b41cc4d6e6a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:80e7d0cc968743d9f09ef1b98e9792f3db96e5bc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}